---

<Base path="/evidence/">
  <PosterBand crumb="Evidence & progress">
    <Fragment slot="title">Follow the records.<br /><em>Hold them to account.</em></Fragment>
    <p slot="intro">
      Our solidarity calls us to act. The records let us examine Arkansas’s choices and check whether officials change them.
    </p>
    <ResearchNav path="/evidence/" />
  </PosterBand>

  <div class="wrap evidence">
    <section class="margin-grid opening" aria-labelledby="claim-title">
      <h2 id="claim-title">Start with the claim</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This archive provides fuller documents behind the financial findings on The issue page. Read the <a
            href="/investments/">dated investment ledger</a
          >, examine <a href="/policy/">each institution’s route to change</a>, and follow the <a href="/progress/"
            >progress record</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          These are selected documents, not a complete release of every agency production. The response dates below come from
          our research records. Agency cover letters are not included.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="index">
      <h2 id="evidence-index-title">Index of documents</h2>
      <p>Ten records, in the order they appear below. Each ID matches the citations in the investment ledger.</p>
      <div class="table-region reflow">
        <table role="table" aria-labelledby="evidence-index-title">
          <thead role="rowgroup">
            <tr role="row">
              <th scope="col" role="columnheader">ID</th>
              <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Record</th>
              <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Document date</th>
              <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Response recorded</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody role="rowgroup">
            {
              index.map((row) => (
                <tr role="row">
                  <th scope="row" role="rowheader">
                    <a class="data idlink" href={`#${row.id}`}>
                      {row.id}
                    </a>
                  </th>
                  <td role="cell" data-label="Record">{row.record}</td>
                  <td role="cell" data-label="Document date">
                    <span class="data">{row.docDate}</span>
                  </td>
                  <td role="cell" data-label="Response recorded">{/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/.test(row.response) ? <span class="data">{row.response}</span> : row.response}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    {
      sources.map((s) => (
        <section class="margin-grid source" id={s.id} aria-labelledby={`${s.id}-title`}>
          <h2 id={`${s.id}-title`}>{s.title}</h2>
          <p class="margin srcid">
            <span class="data">{s.id}</span>
          </p>
          <p class="provenance dated">{s.dated}</p>
          <div class="prose">
            {s.about.map((p) => (
              <p>{p}</p>
            ))}
            <p>
              <strong>Source location:</strong> {s.location}
            </p>
            {s.correction && <p class="provenance" set:html={s.correction} />}
            <p>
              <a class="go doc" href={s.pdf}>
                {s.pdf.startsWith("http") ? <Icon name="external" /> : <Icon name="download" />}Read the document (PDF)
              </a>
            </p>
            <details class="disclosure">
              <summary>
                Redactions and provenance <Icon name="plus" />
              </summary>
              <div class="panel">
                <p>{s.redactions}</p>
                <p>
                  Public-copy SHA-256: <code class="hash">{s.hash}</code>
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>
          {s.figure && (
            <div class="wide">
              <RecordFigure image={s.figure.image} href={s.figure.href} alt={s.figure.alt} label="Excerpt">
                {s.figure.caption}
              </RecordFigure>
            </div>
          )}
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <section class="margin-grid opening" aria-labelledby="text-title">
      <h2 id="text-title">Read the financial evidence in text</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The redacted PDFs show the original document pages as images. You can also read their financial findings in the <a
            href="/investments/">investment ledger</a
          >, including dates, amounts, interest rates, maturities and source locations. The ATRS email is also readable
          directly as text.
        </p>
        <p>
          APERS’s November 6 correspondence identifies an initial purchase on October 15, asks for the term sheet, and
          discusses statement frequency and accounting setup. The attached advice records a $15 million initial subscription
          and a $15 million holding on October 20. Its 4.06% coupon and October 1, 2027 maturity describe the bond, not a
          comparison with other investments.
        </p>
        <p>
          The BNY report for APERS, dated September 7, 2026 and marked preliminary, lists two State of Israel bonds: $10 million
          at 4.67% maturing August 1, 2028, and the $15 million bond at 4.06% maturing October 1, 2027. Its Israel Bonds
          subtotal is $25 million at cost and at market value.
        </p>
        <p>
          ATRS’s activity report shows its $50 million internal transfer to the Reams account completed with a January 2, 2026
          settlement date. The purchase confirmation shows a $9.9 million State of Israel bond, CUSIP 46515DSQ6, issued
          February 15, 2026 at 4.93% and maturing February 1, 2031. The July 31 worksheet lists that bond at $9.9 million par
          beside U.S. Treasury notes and cash. The manager’s second-quarter report states a long-term objective of a laddered
          Israel Bonds portfolio, buying no more than $10 million in a calendar year.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Treasury cashflow sheet labels its period January 29, 2026 to January 28, 2027. It records a February 2 coupon of
          $17,013.6986 in the workbook (displayed rounded to $17,013.70), a $5 million final-maturity entry, and a $5 million
          inventory adjustment. Its projected-cashflow heading remains visible; the sheet alone does not prove bank receipt.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="margin-grid opening" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <h2 id="method-title">About these documents</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We preserve the original records and provide copies with sensitive details removed. Redactions remove personal
          contact information, account details, and processing identifiers. We do not reconstruct missing material or add
          highlights to source evidence. Any highlighting already present in an agency production remains part of that source.
        </p>
        <p>
          A holding, purchase, authorization, and payment to an investment manager establish different things. We explain what
          each document shows, what it leaves unanswered, and where we offer an interpretation.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/about/#corrections">Flag an error or request source context</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <CloseStrip />
</Base>

<style>
  .evidence {
    padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-8);
  }
  .opening {
    padding-top: var(--s-7);
  }
  .opening .prose,
  .source .prose {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }
  .index {
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
  }
  .index > p {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
    max-width: 40em;
  }
  .idlink {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .source {
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
    padding-top: var(--s-5);
    border-top: 0.5rem solid var(--olive);
  }
  .source > h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }
  .srcid .data {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .dated {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .doc .icon {
    width: 1.1em;
    height: 1.1em;
  }
  .hash {
    word-break: break-all;
    font-size: 0.82em;
    display: inline;
  }
  .wide {
    max-width: 62rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .margin-grid > .wide {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
